  "raw": " could \"very easily make\" a tactical U-turn when parliament resumes.\nThe DA has faced consecutive ouster bids by its federal executive council at its January national conferences, but the party muddied the waters at the meeting earlier this month, when it allowed a vote on the bill even though there was no supporting party motion or rally in favour of it.\nThe party's federal chairperson James Selfe said the motion was voted for by activists and volunteers, and not for \"outright endorsement\". He claimed that official party support for the bill would cause a massive split and cause \"acute headaches\" for Speaker Baleka Mbete when parliament resumes next week.\nAt the weekend Selfe released the party's federal council decision-making documents, which revealed there had been no motions submitted on the bill or any official party support during the February 11 meeting. However, as previously reported, the whip office allegedly admitted to negotiating a deal with the EFF to vote to continue debating the minor",
